        "severity": "medium",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "EEPROM length from driver not bounded by 1024-byte buffer",
        "explanation": "eeprom_info.length is taken from module_info.eeprom_len, which is reported by the driver. The destination buffer is a fixed EEPROM_DUMP_CHUNKSIZE (1024) bytes. If a module reports a larger EEPROM, rte_eth_dev_get_module_eeprom can write past the stack buffer. rte_hexdump would then read past it too.",
        "suggestion": "Check module_info.eeprom_len against sizeof(bytes_eeprom). Either reject larger values or read in chunks of EEPROM_DUMP_CHUNKSIZE, advancing the offset each time.",
        "evidence": "eeprom_info.length = module_info.eeprom_len;",
        "confidence": 0.55,
